er/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/11/11fd2ec491cdd866338cdee26092668315c872558b4b000608dd21f7e6dd701e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708281} {:answer/id #uuid "3c23b009-07b3-515c-a3a0-22413feda69d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/12/124001c6fa8e74c0b4576b08eb22e129aa7ddb9081fa8c3a120c480a49b31ce7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708282} {:answer/id #uuid "a3a5c3c4-1388-533d-9a92-36877c32babe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/0c/0c17016c6470aeab549495c4cd7961ec7ad8ca4552fb1a12b0a6f377496f2101.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708292} {:answer/id #uuid "c6889d19-a66e-53c7-954f-2ac3c104286d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/bb/bb83524be625efee137ead1baaddd2a81f0215f0c12a1c804fecbe939a135c00.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708298}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708292} :answer-field/id #uuid "27585286-79f8-5277-8555-34b24dda8d64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d0506834-ad57-5a8f-aa8d-234c8e5c5e1c" :question/problem "The labeled lines are level curves of a function $f(x,y)$.\n\n![Labeled level curves](images/6d/6dd252f5ac4ae31575c0c3c88da96eb31dd8ffd57f30c939a68b68b084a7d6d0.png)\n\nRecall that gradient vectors are **perpendicular** to level curves and point toward **increasing** function values. Which diagram could show its gradient vector field? Arrows show directions only." :question/worked-solution "The level curves are parallel straight lines. A normal is proportional to $(-1,1)$. Use the labels to choose its sense: moving in that direction raises the labels, so it is the gradient direction. Tangent arrows fail perpendicularity; the opposite normal points toward smaller labels.\n\n![Matching contours and gradient directions](images/de/de4c7bf8194d85c42d462137191b2c3164ea65c6d3f802623cfd4f1949ca0bb9.png)\n\nTherefore choose this diagram:\n\n![Correct diagram](images/0c/0c17016c6470aeab549495c4cd7961ec7ad8ca4552fb1a12b0a6f377496f2101.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708439 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03714e10-40ec-52c5-86fd-ad5f810e257e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac92" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708431} {:answer/id #uuid "11000a05-85cd-5ba7-9261-69a1b1419021" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708435} {:answer/id #uuid "208f74db-288a-5489-9fc9-3876e45c1522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708438} {:answer/id #uuid "8c76e16b-0493-5392-a364-635a23e6c0ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708443} {:answer/id #uuid "cb67a7f0-b204-5cfd-86b2-9a7f91be5e59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708448}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708435} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf125840-a2d3-543f-bbaf-6a6576c18305" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4432a0b0-7dd3-5474-a534-48b20a7af6e3" :question/problem "![](images/60/6087da076e65bda5240c428ff67c570ad59ae9a8e5a5a3c9e8406184998de56a.png)\n\nThe path $C_1$ is the line segment from $O(0,0)$ to $A(1,0)$, and $C_2$ is the line segment from $A(1,0)$ to $B(0,-2)$. Traverse $C=C_1\\cup C_2$ in that order.\n\nLet $\\mathbf F(x,y)=(x+y)\\mathbf i+(2x-2y)\\mathbf j$. Given that\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=-\\frac{11}{2},\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$.\n\nFor $C_1$, use $\\mathbf r_1(t)=t\\mathbf i+0\\mathbf j$, $0\\le t\\le1$." :question/worked-solution "Split the integral over the two oriented pieces:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r.\n$$\n\nThe second integral is given, so calculate only the first. The supplied parametrization runs from $O$ to $A$. Along $C_1$, $x=t$ and $y=0$, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r_1(t))&=t\\mathbf i+2t\\mathbf j,\\\\\\mathbf r_1'(t)&=\\mathbf i,\\\\\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r_1(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r_1'(t)&=t(1)+2t(0)=t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_0^1t\\,\\mathrm dt=\\left[\\frac{t^2}{2}\\right]_0^1=\\frac12.\n$$\n\nAdd this to the supplied value for $C_2$:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\frac12-\\frac{11}{2}=-5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708440 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06eb73e0-e37d-5986-b236-df8f9d3f97b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708432} {:answer/id #uuid "0e1454e9-25ea-5eff-881c-5cc58b0b67ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708433} {:answer/id #uuid "0fdd0ade-f6c3-56b9-a633-baa10d51f5b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708434} {:answer/id #uuid "17be7573-6095-5b03-8297-9a185819fec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708437} {:answer/id #uuid "9716cf4f-bd0e-5106-8b54-08ef02b7a50d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708444}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708433} :answer-field/id #uuid "17ade847-c84b-5712-bf4d-33a27809f7d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708436}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "470e832b-a4fb-5107-87f6-22a4b6d4ce9e" :question/problem "![](images/87/87182d625f4e669a6b2791a17f3e12c34922043b8f3deefd6b2473e8fb529886.png)\n\nThe path $C_1$ is the line segment from $O(0,0)$ to $A(2,0)$, and $C_2$ is the section of the parabola $y=4-x^2$ from $A(2,0)$ to $B(0,4)$. Traverse $C=C_1\\cup C_2$ in that order.\n\nLet $\\mathbf F(x,y)=(x+y)\\mathbf i+2x\\mathbf j$. Given that\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=2,\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$." :question/worked-solution "Use the supplied integral for the straight segment and calculate the curved contribution:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r.\n$$\n\nTo use an increasing $x$ parameter, first parametrize the reversed curve $-C_2$, from $B$ to $A$:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=t\\mathbf i+(4-t^2)\\mathbf j,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le2.\n$$\n\nThis runs from $\\mathbf r(0)=(0,4)$ to $\\mathbf r(2)=(2,0)$, opposite to $C_2$. Along this curve,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))&=(t+4-t^2)\\mathbf i+2t\\mathbf j,\\\\\\mathbf r'(t)&=\\mathbf i-2t\\mathbf j,\\\\\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r'(t)&=(t+4-t^2)(1)+(2t)(-2t)\\\\&=4+t-5t^2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{-C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=\\int_0^2(4+t-5t^2)\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\&=\\left[4t+\\frac{t^2}{2}-\\frac53t^3\\right]_0^2\\\\&=8+2-\\frac{40}{3}=-\\frac{10}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReverse the sign to recover the required direction, then add the given contribution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=-\\int_{-C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\frac{10}{3},\\\\\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=2+\\frac{10}{3}=\\frac{16}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, $x=t$, $y=4-t^2$ with limits from $2$ to $0$ gives the required orientation directly."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708445 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48cd8714-ae26-5491-aefc-a9b7503fc03e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708441} {:answer/id #uuid "c32b30e4-f9a7-5a3e-a8f9-96f7c93277a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708447} {:answer/id #uuid "dbe4d939-c62c-553a-a0cd-4504466d2985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708449} {:answer/id #uuid "fb24f18a-c281-59a5-a613-81bbf6c1c39c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708450} {:answer/id #uuid "fe1bc69d-0572-59da-897b-3c7b6705e590" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708451}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708441} :answer-field/id #uuid "561ea4bd-5566-5cb3-af1a-c6414dbaf669" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708442}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "abcbe4ec-e19e-530e-aa39-27c53737dc3d" :question/problem "![](images/04/0457cb819e6f39ef9c0978e356cff788e1cf5edbef9cbf844a054ab777b70eac.png)\n\nThe path $C_1$ is the line segment from $A(-2,0)$ to $B(0,1)$, and $C_2$ is the line segment from $B(0,1)$ to $D(1,1)$. Traverse $C=C_1\\cup C_2$ in that order.\n\nLet $\\mathbf F(x,y)=(x-2y)\\mathbf i+(2x+y)\\mathbf j$. Given that\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=-\\frac32,\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$." :question/worked-solution "Use additivity over the two pieces:\n\n$$\n\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r.\n$$\n\nThe second integral is given. Parametrize the first segment from $A$ to $B$ by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_1(t)&=\\langle-2,0\\rangle+t\\bigl(\\langle0,1\\rangle-\\langle-2,0\\rangle\\bigr)\\\\&=(-2+2t)\\mathbf i+t\\mathbf j,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $t=0$ we are at $A$, and at $t=1$ we are at $B$, as required. Writing $\\mathbf F=P\\mathbf i+Q\\mathbf j$, substitute $x=-2+2t$ and $y=t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\mathbf r_1(t))&=(-2+2t)-2t=-2,\\\\Q(\\mathbf r_1(t))&=2(-2+2t)+t=-4+5t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r_1(t))&=-2\\mathbf i+(-4+5t)\\mathbf j,\\\\\\mathbf r_1'(t)&=2\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j,\\\\\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r_1(t))\\cdot\\mathbf r_1'(t)&=(-2)(2)+(-4+5t)(1)\\\\&=-8+5t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate and then add the known contribution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=\\int_0^1(-8+5t)\\,\\mathrm dt\\\\&=\\left[-8t+\\frac52t^2\\right]_0^1=-\\frac{11}{2},\\\\\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=-\\frac{11}{2}-\\frac32=-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708455 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "184d96c7-4d57-5d27-b76c-c57ad34b9e2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708453}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708453} :answer-field/id #uuid "38fa8085-196f-5950-b4f4-bf7733b22c92" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708454}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4d443258-293e-5ae5-87c4-87cda970c1b2" :question/problem "![](images/06/06f90fbcd495493bcbab5bd9aa0109e89a6ac092aabb6949c3385bce4d543cb1.png)\n\nThe arrows show the orientations of $C_1$, $C_2$, and $C_3$. The closed path $C$ follows $A\\to B\\to C\\to A$ **counterclockwise**. For the same continuous vector field $\\mathbf F$, you are given\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=6,\\\\\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=-3,\\\\\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the integral along $C_2$ in the direction of its arrows.\n\n$\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=$ {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "The traversal $A\\to B$ reverses $C_1$, $B\\to C$ follows $C_2$, and $C\\to A$ reverses $C_3$. Thus, by additivity and orientation reversal,\n\n$$\n\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=-\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the three given values:\n\n$$\n6=-(-3)+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-2=1+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r.\n$$\n\nSubtract $1$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=5.\n$$\n\nThis is already the direction requested; no further reversal is needed."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708457 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c572b3f1-cc36-553c-a28a-d0c9afde01dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708463}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708463} :answer-field/id #uuid "a11cccbe-8582-5672-8075-5420d99ee36f" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8079d3e6-95e5-5be5-a139-0e610b5f72f8" :question/problem "![](images/3e/3e0e8cf7cb700cb6d9ee074a0bb3eac1c82b24229b8d66e636121e53998fee7e.png)\n\nThe arrows show the orientations of the five segments. The same continuous vector field $\\mathbf F$ is used for every integral. Let $L_1$ follow $A\\to B\\to C\\to A$, and let $L_2$ follow $A\\to D\\to C\\to A$. You are given\n\n$$\n\\int_{L_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=3,\\qquad \\int_{L_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=-5.\n$$\n\nThe closed path $C$ follows the **outer boundary** $A\\to B\\to C\\to D\\to A$, counterclockwise. Evaluate its line integral.\n\n$\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=$ {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Write $I_j=\\int_{C_j}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$ for each segment in its arrow direction. The first triangular loop follows $C_1$, reverses $C_2$, and reverses the diagonal $C_5$. The second follows $C_4$, reverses $C_3$, and also reverses $C_5$. Hence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{L_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=I_1-I_2-I_5=3,\\\\\\int_{L_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=I_4-I_3-I_5=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe outer boundary follows $C_1$, reverses $C_2$, follows $C_3$, and reverses $C_4$, so\n\n$$\n\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=I_1-I_2+I_3-I_4.\n$$\n\nSubtract the second loop integral from the first. This reverses the second loop; their diagonal contributions then cancel:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=(I_1-I_2-I_5)-(I_4-I_3-I_5)\\\\&=\\int_{L_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{L_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\\\&=3-(-5)\\\\&=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two given loop integrals would traverse the diagonal twice in the same direction. Subtracting removes it. A closed path alone does not make a vector line integral zero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708458 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c177aa5-3f93-5176-bc57-6de2d25ec6f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708452} {:answer/id #uuid "4ffe9032-87e6-59d8-bac7-2c6944d92c2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708456} {:answer/id #uuid "971b1375-57e4-5d5c-bc6b-3f7c348e2578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708459} {:answer/id #uuid "b8714dcc-079c-50a0-931b-8df03e62258b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708461} {:answer/id #uuid "f211fe50-8881-599d-85b3-b282ec9b689a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708464}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708464} :answer-field/id #uuid "b920d18e-dfd2-5fd7-a5ef-c8692adb7835" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708462}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8e22c1f0-3a76-538e-8b30-88b473af30ed" :question/problem "![](images/0a/0a6607e7239dda7b14a9164bb934556a0ac1a49778e791f6a3ceadebf6e11638.png)\n\nThe arrows show the orientations of $C_1$, $C_2$, and $C_3$. Let $C$ be the closed polygonal path $A\\to B\\to C\\to A$, traversed **counterclockwise**. Which expression equals\n\n$$\n\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n$$\n\nfor an arbitrary continuous vector field $\\mathbf F$ on these segments?" :question/worked-solution "Follow the required traversal around the triangle. The segment $A\\to B$ follows $C_1$, the segment $B\\to C$ reverses $C_2$, and the segment $C\\to A$ follows $C_3$.\n\nAdditivity gives\n\n$$\n\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{-C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n$$\n\nReversing a path changes the sign of its vector line integral, so\n\n$$\n\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r.\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708524 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d35cbe66-2210-557c-9b23-6eef3e9d111a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3 x y}{9 x^{2} y^{2} z^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708534}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708534} :answer-field/id #uuid "00bdaa9e-ec48-5572-b828-b4aec8bfc225" :answer-field/key "component-z" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708508} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48df9813-7e27-5f8a-bac9-4682750c2e22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3 x z}{9 x^{2} y^{2} z^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708517}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708517} :answer-field/id #uuid "24563054-5195-5c78-b9d9-2e1c82be4ae1" :answer-field/key "component-y" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708514} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ba257c9-d5ea-55c4-9a43-dee8d2c0e3b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3 y z}{9 x^{2} y^{2} z^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708511}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708511} :answer-field/id #uuid "f47ed2af-b14f-5938-8b04-6d8a6e29d145" :answer-field/key "component-x" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708540}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "804f5e08-0b66-5874-a332-d795530b0194" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\arctan{\\left(3 x y z \\right)} + 2$.\n\nEnter its component functions:\n\n$\\nabla f(x,y,z)=$ {{component-x}} $\\,i$ $+$ {{component-y}} $\\,j$ $+$ {{component-z}} $\\,k$." :question/worked-solution "Compute each partial derivative while holding the other variables constant. The additive constant has zero partial derivatives.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}(x,y,z)&=\\frac{1}{1+(3 x y z)^2}\\cdot 3 y z \\\\ &=\\frac{3 y z}{9 x^{2} y^{2} z^{2} + 1} \\\\ f_{y}(x,y,z)&=\\frac{1}{1+(3 x y z)^2}\\cdot 3 x z \\\\ &=\\frac{3 x z}{9 x^{2} y^{2} z^{2} + 1} \\\\ f_{z}(x,y,z)&=\\frac{1}{1+(3 x y z)^2}\\cdot 3 x y \\\\ &=\\frac{3 x y}{9 x^{2} y^{2} z^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssemble the components in coordinate order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla f(x,y,z)&=\\left(\\frac{3 y z}{9 x^{2} y^{2} z^{2} + 1}\\right)\\,i \\\\ &+\\left(\\frac{3 x z}{9 x^{2} y^{2} z^{2} + 1}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(\\frac{3 x y}{9 x^{2} y^{2} z^{2} + 1}\\right)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708527 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69e17397-dd04-5f00-b74f-48fadb2d42a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\ln{\\left(- 2 x + y \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708521}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708521} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d4d145c-05f6-561f-8431-bb719300e6a3" :answer-field/key "component-z" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708516} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9ab5d59-8829-5b86-9cc5-4181244a8f48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{z}{- 2 x + y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708532}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708532} :answer-field/id #uuid "af8009a6-d015-5498-b08c-0c1a60221e3c" :answer-field/key "component-y" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708526} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b68584cf-8d5e-5d30-8aed-296d007739f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{2 z}{- 2 x + y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708528}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708528} :answer-field/id #uuid "f97fd1b7-4479-567a-9c1d-fafd81f1884e" :answer-field/key "component-x" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708541}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b296aa77-2a7d-51e1-86d5-1af12cca0b78" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=z \\ln{\\left(- 2 x + y \\right)}$ on $- 2 x + y>0$.\n\nEnter its component functions:\n\n$\\nabla f(x,y,z)=$ {{component-x}} $\\,i$ $+$ {{component-y}} $\\,j$ $+$ {{component-z}} $\\,k$." :question/worked-solution "Compute each partial derivative while holding the other variables constant.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}(x,y,z)&=z\\cdot\\frac{1}{- 2 x + y}\\cdot(-2) \\\\ &=- \\frac{2 z}{- 2 x + y} \\\\ f_{y}(x,y,z)&=z\\cdot\\frac{1}{- 2 x + y}\\cdot1 \\\\ &=\\frac{z}{- 2 x + y} \\\\ f_{z}(x,y,z)&=1\\cdot \\ln{\\left(- 2 x + y \\right)} \\\\ &=\\ln{\\left(- 2 x + y \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssemble the components in coordinate order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla f(x,y,z)&=\\left(- \\frac{2 z}{- 2 x + y}\\right)\\,i \\\\ &+\\left(\\frac{z}{- 2 x + y}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(\\ln{\\left(- 2 x + y \\right)}\\right)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708533 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "509cbf5c-83fc-5eab-bb66-248cd1938fc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 x y - 3 z^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708518}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708518} :answer-field/id #uuid "03ade6d0-096b-5877-96cf-7a1fcfad3d9a" :answer-field/key "component-y" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708509} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2194af72-1e80-50cd-a858-d9b4cec5830e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 8 x^{3} z + y^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708513}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708513} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d7fe260-f592-5dd9-a8dd-9758cbb68c29" :answer-field/key "component-x" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708510} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e86ebbbd-af69-596b-9096-56e1e8e712de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 2 x^{4} - 9 y z^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708538}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708538} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a7ed434-c1d2-58dc-a774-6bbf2f43f625" :answer-field/key "component-z" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d10ff71a-7047-55b3-b2c9-a49e6a54a369" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=- 2 x^{4} z + x y^{2} - 3 y z^{3}$.\n\nEnter its component functions:\n\n$\\nabla f(x,y,z)=$ {{component-x}} $\\,i$ $+$ {{component-y}} $\\,j$ $+$ {{component-z}} $\\,k$." :question/worked-solution "Compute each partial derivative while holding the other variables constant.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}(x,y,z)&=- 8 x^{3} z + y^{2} \\\\ &=- 8 x^{3} z + y^{2} \\\\ f_{y}(x,y,z)&=2 x y - 3 z^{3} \\\\ &=2 x y - 3 z^{3} \\\\ f_{z}(x,y,z)&=- 2 x^{4} - 9 y z^{2} \\\\ &=- 2 x^{4} - 9 y z^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssemble the components in coordinate order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla f(x,y,z)&=\\left(- 8 x^{3} z + y^{2}\\right)\\,i \\\\ &+\\left(2 x y - 3 z^{3}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(- 2 x^{4} - 9 y z^{2}\\right)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708537 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c8f218c-d635-5a4c-96e4-f2245352c708" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 2 \\cos{\\left(x z - 2 y \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708512}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708512} :answer-field/id #uuid "53f5b2b4-7d46-531e-9000-ed69bf7fb06a" :answer-field/key "component-y" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708519} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c249e769-c998-5c1e-8277-d62c6767da09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z \\cos{\\left(x z - 2 y \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708531}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708531} :answer-field/id #uuid "631b9837-8d11-59d7-9c64-8f6582f792c1" :answer-field/key "component-x" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708520} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dacdb3b3-4aca-52dd-af74-482658ae257d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x \\cos{\\left(x z - 2 y \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708536}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708536} :answer-field/id #uuid "7da39544-24fe-5b08-bfdc-627c3abb00d3" :answer-field/key "component-z" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dd0032c3-a5ea-5ed9-bf13-d1d8c927f939" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\sin{\\left(x z - 2 y \\right)}$.\n\nEnter its component functions:\n\n$\\nabla f(x,y,z)=$ {{component-x}} $\\,i$ $+$ {{component-y}} $\\,j$ $+$ {{component-z}} $\\,k$." :question/worked-solution "Compute each partial derivative while holding the other variables constant.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}(x,y,z)&=\\cos{\\left(x z - 2 y \\right)}\\cdot\\left(z\\right) \\\\ &=z \\cos{\\left(x z - 2 y \\right)} \\\\ f_{y}(x,y,z)&=\\cos{\\left(x z - 2 y \\right)}\\cdot\\left(-2\\right) \\\\ &=- 2 \\cos{\\left(x z - 2 y \\right)} \\\\ f_{z}(x,y,z)&=\\cos{\\left(x z - 2 y \\right)}\\cdot\\left(x\\right) \\\\ &=x \\cos{\\left(x z - 2 y \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssemble the components in coordinate order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla f(x,y,z)&=\\left(z \\cos{\\left(x z - 2 y \\right)}\\right)\\,i \\\\ &+\\left(- 2 \\cos{\\left(x z - 2 y \\right)}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(x \\cos{\\left(x z - 2 y \\right)}\\right)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708539 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3173c660-8174-5081-8ade-1439c02458cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3 y}{\\sqrt{3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2} + 2 z^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708515}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708515} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d914c52-a58e-549f-920d-009ad8d94f86" :answer-field/key "component-y" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708525} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfe9f4f2-60d1-5af4-b866-078db4a03614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3 x}{\\sqrt{3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2} + 2 z^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708529}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708529} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfeb2d6a-2313-5376-806a-d47fe6fdd4c4" :answer-field/key "component-x" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708530} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5d6a748-202c-531a-9ea0-b133be0cef7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 z}{\\sqrt{3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2} + 2 z^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708535}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708535} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb54883d-67e0-58ed-85e5-c98114757623" :answer-field/key "component-z" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708542}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f1590130-c651-58db-8271-9b4cb2c89071" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2} + 2 z^{2}} - 2$ on $(x,y,z)\\ne(0,0,0)$.\n\nEnter its component functions:\n\n$\\nabla f(x,y,z)=$ {{component-x}} $\\,i$ $+$ {{component-y}} $\\,j$ $+$ {{component-z}} $\\,k$." :question/worked-solution "Compute each partial derivative while holding the other variables constant. The additive constant has zero partial derivatives.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}(x,y,z)&=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2} + 2 z^{2}}}\\cdot 6 x \\\\ &=\\frac{3 x}{\\sqrt{3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2} + 2 z^{2}}} \\\\ f_{y}(x,y,z)&=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2} + 2 z^{2}}}\\cdot 6 y \\\\ &=\\frac{3 y}{\\sqrt{3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2} + 2 z^{2}}} \\\\ f_{z}(x,y,z)&=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2} + 2 z^{2}}}\\cdot 4 z \\\\ &=\\frac{2 z}{\\sqrt{3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2} + 2 z^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssemble the components in coordinate order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla f(x,y,z)&=\\left(\\frac{3 x}{\\sqrt{3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2} + 2 z^{2}}}\\right)\\,i \\\\ &+\\left(\\frac{3 y}{\\sqrt{3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2} + 2 z^{2}}}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(\\frac{2 z}{\\sqrt{3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2} + 2 z^{2}}}\\right)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708561 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c0cafa6-ae1f-5ec1-8931-5d9238d778ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 y^{2} \\cos{\\left(x - 2 y z \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708562}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708562} :answer-field/id #uuid "35d199d4-e03a-536f-9c50-918f06afb96d" :answer-field/key "component-z" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708552} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "163acd6e-90da-5603-9623-edf9655ea1d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- y \\cos{\\left(x - 2 y z \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708546}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708546} :answer-field/id #uuid "4658bcf4-db80-5b0d-8c76-0fbcb5dc6f82" :answer-field/key "component-x" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708554} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7d1afed-cc5b-524c-9c1c-45a65379fe82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 y z \\cos{\\left(x - 2 y z \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(x - 2 y z \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708571}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708571} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a9cf26f-176c-5cd9-8d5c-6e07c480b65b" :answer-field/key "component-y" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708556}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "926a6588-92d0-580c-ac02-d43ed7469e63" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=- y \\sin{\\left(x - 2 y z \\right)}$.\n\nEnter its component functions:\n\n$\\nabla f(x,y,z)=$ {{component-x}} $\\,i$ $+$ {{component-y}} $\\,j$ $+$ {{component-z}} $\\,k$." :question/worked-solution "Compute each partial derivative while holding the other variables constant. In the $y$ derivative, both the coordinate prefactor and the argument depend on $y$, so use both the product rule and the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}(x,y,z)&=y\\cdot \\cos{\\left(x - 2 y z \\right)}\\cdot\\left(-1\\right) \\\\ &=- y \\cos{\\left(x - 2 y z \\right)} \\\\ f_{y}(x,y,z)&=- \\sin{\\left(x - 2 y z \\right)}+y\\cdot \\cos{\\left(x - 2 y z \\right)}\\cdot\\left(2 z\\right) \\\\ &=2 y z \\cos{\\left(x - 2 y z \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(x - 2 y z \\right)} \\\\ f_{z}(x,y,z)&=y\\cdot \\cos{\\left(x - 2 y z \\right)}\\cdot\\left(2 y\\right) \\\\ &=2 y^{2} \\cos{\\left(x - 2 y z \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssemble the components in coordinate order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla f(x,y,z)&=\\left(- y \\cos{\\left(x - 2 y z \\right)}\\right)\\,i \\\\ &+\\left(2 y z \\cos{\\left(x - 2 y z \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(x - 2 y z \\right)}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(2 y^{2} \\cos{\\left(x - 2 y z \\right)}\\right)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708563 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aecd24a-99db-53a3-8c0b-568f326deb4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z^{2} e^{x z - 2 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708548}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708548} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b9e7251-bb6d-57a9-9e0a-d251abc555a4" :answer-field/key "component-x" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708550} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e0942e8-49f7-57e9-9dfa-0f7149e37185" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x z e^{x z - 2 y} + e^{x z - 2 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708555}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708555} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b647dab-2106-52e1-b28f-682cb9cfb531" :answer-field/key "component-z" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708557} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35b7aa32-6cea-58a5-96aa-d276c76a0eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 2 z e^{x z - 2 y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708551}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708551} :answer-field/id #uuid "701ea258-f61d-5507-adf3-1540a9932b0a" :answer-field/key "component-y" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708558}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b2ea45e9-4b27-5130-b46e-42e627d0bed6" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=z e^{x z - 2 y}$.\n\nEnter its component functions:\n\n$\\nabla f(x,y,z)=$ {{component-x}} $\\,i$ $+$ {{component-y}} $\\,j$ $+$ {{component-z}} $\\,k$." :question/worked-solution "Compute each partial derivative while holding the other variables constant. In the $z$ derivative, both the coordinate prefactor and the argument depend on $z$, so use both the product rule and the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}(x,y,z)&=z\\cdot e^{x z - 2 y}\\cdot\\left(z\\right) \\\\ &=z^{2} e^{x z - 2 y} \\\\ f_{y}(x,y,z)&=z\\cdot e^{x z - 2 y}\\cdot\\left(-2\\right) \\\\ &=- 2 z e^{x z - 2 y} \\\\ f_{z}(x,y,z)&=e^{x z - 2 y}+z\\cdot e^{x z - 2 y}\\cdot\\left(x\\right) \\\\ &=x z e^{x z - 2 y} + e^{x z - 2 y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssemble the components in coordinate order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla f(x,y,z)&=\\left(z^{2} e^{x z - 2 y}\\right)\\,i \\\\ &+\\left(- 2 z e^{x z - 2 y}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(x z e^{x z - 2 y} + e^{x z - 2 y}\\right)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708568 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2cd4bd3-4f31-5c5d-b04f-6353e9249a0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 2 y e^{- 2 x + y z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708566}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708566} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dbaca98-e33c-5102-a2ab-76667c0a11e2" :answer-field/key "component-x" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708544} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1085e8a9-915c-5b63-b216-fd621826a999" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^{2} e^{- 2 x + y z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708545}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708545} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c0eec04-72a2-54c4-b71d-471afe428b40" :answer-field/key "component-z" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708560} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2786f6a-555b-57b0-90a6-0b685b680c56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y z e^{- 2 x + y z} + e^{- 2 x + y z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708567}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708567} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed77e3fb-d0fd-5e74-9fdf-691ee7c04bda" :answer-field/key "component-y" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ec9abd7b-14b3-5750-b0c4-7fce8e79e34f" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=y e^{- 2 x + y z}$.\n\nEnter its component functions:\n\n$\\nabla f(x,y,z)=$ {{component-x}} $\\,i$ $+$ {{component-y}} $\\,j$ $+$ {{component-z}} $\\,k$." :question/worked-solution "Compute each partial derivative while holding the other variables constant. In the $y$ derivative, both the coordinate prefactor and the argument depend on $y$, so use both the product rule and the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}(x,y,z)&=y\\cdot e^{- 2 x + y z}\\cdot\\left(-2\\right) \\\\ &=- 2 y e^{- 2 x + y z} \\\\ f_{y}(x,y,z)&=e^{- 2 x + y z}+y\\cdot e^{- 2 x + y z}\\cdot\\left(z\\right) \\\\ &=y z e^{- 2 x + y z} + e^{- 2 x + y z} \\\\ f_{z}(x,y,z)&=y\\cdot e^{- 2 x + y z}\\cdot\\left(y\\right) \\\\ &=y^{2} e^{- 2 x + y z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssemble the components in coordinate order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla f(x,y,z)&=\\left(- 2 y e^{- 2 x + y z}\\right)\\,i \\\\ &+\\left(y z e^{- 2 x + y z} + e^{- 2 x + y z}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(y^{2} e^{- 2 x + y z}\\right)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708570 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78010af9-5c15-5bb6-82fa-393888845178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x z \\cos{\\left(x z + y \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(x z + y \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708559}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708559} :answer-field/id #uuid "164fc709-713f-50ed-9d8c-d29b7532968c" :answer-field/key "component-x" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708547} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a510cad-0a21-5ae6-806f-e85283c097d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x^{2} \\cos{\\left(x z + y \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708549}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708549} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3dc1ebe-0b72-5b16-bfe8-0d53e3405717" :answer-field/key "component-z" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708564} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45297317-ecd1-57ff-8517-858691520026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x \\cos{\\left(x z + y \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708553}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708553} :answer-field/id #uuid "b831d81a-b152-55ac-a5f2-86e08f40364e" :answer-field/key "component-y" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708565}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f2ed4f0d-cdb3-5df9-8c8f-2e126bb21a42" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=x \\sin{\\left(x z + y \\right)}$.\n\nEnter its component functions:\n\n$\\nabla f(x,y,z)=$ {{component-x}} $\\,i$ $+$ {{component-y}} $\\,j$ $+$ {{component-z}} $\\,k$." :question/worked-solution "Compute each partial derivative while holding the other variables constant. In the $x$ derivative, both the coordinate prefactor and the argument depend on $x$, so use both the product rule and the chain rule.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_{x}(x,y,z)&=\\sin{\\left(x z + y \\right)}+x\\cdot \\cos{\\left(x z + y \\right)}\\cdot\\left(z\\right) \\\\ &=x z \\cos{\\left(x z + y \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(x z + y \\right)} \\\\ f_{y}(x,y,z)&=x\\cdot \\cos{\\left(x z + y \\right)}\\cdot\\left(1\\right) \\\\ &=x \\cos{\\left(x z + y \\right)} \\\\ f_{z}(x,y,z)&=x\\cdot \\cos{\\left(x z + y \\right)}\\cdot\\left(x\\right) \\\\ &=x^{2} \\cos{\\left(x z + y \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssemble the components in coordinate order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla f(x,y,z)&=\\left(x z \\cos{\\left(x z + y \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(x z + y \\right)}\\right)\\,i \\\\ &+\\left(x \\cos{\\left(x z + y \\right)}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(x^{2} \\cos{\\left(x z + y \\right)}\\right)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708636 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1110e83b-f493-5851-bc8a-bda9dbc0355b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708639} {:answer/id #uuid "a6be2a1b-ef81-577e-af77-9b96bdd4f48a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708658} {:answer/id #uuid "b38f7a44-fd58-5cdc-8f6c-4a3d3ba5d263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708661} {:answer/id #uuid "ef11cdc0-8d16-5561-a486-ad6a13cd68a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708668} {:answer/id #uuid "f0c8586d-7ad6-5fbc-971a-227685851c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708669}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708668} :answer-field/id #uuid "5db1de62-1d50-5f76-abbf-097b5005aea8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "001737b0-20b4-57ab-8d0d-a5cb7a4e0884" :question/problem "![Directed segments: C_1: B to A; C_2: B to C; C_3: C to A](images/ec/ec44d8735e7e8ffb111f974314816d97f48c9b9f9f04e84d859ebb0da88b5d70.png)\n\nThe arrows show the orientations of the segments. The same continuous vector field $\\mathbf F$ is used throughout. The closed path $C$ follows $A\\to C\\to B\\to A$ **clockwise**. Which expression equals the following line integral?\n\n$$\n\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "Trace the requested traversal. $C_1$ is followed. $C_2$ is reversed. $C_3$ is reversed. Reversal negates a vector line integral, and additivity gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{-C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{-C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\\\&=\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708649 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "182e01e0-a3c2-5770-bf53-e73408d17150" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708640} {:answer/id #uuid "94b4beee-4695-5ccb-98aa-e6dbab47012f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708654} {:answer/id #uuid "ad99cee6-7717-5fea-8b37-62f819769d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708660} {:answer/id #uuid "bef67deb-1c88-50d9-97de-cb0ded1fc40c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708662} {:answer/id #uuid "e71259fb-6a10-53ec-b996-c956766c38bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708667}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708662} :answer-field/id #uuid "c355a782-2a92-5d60-930d-ad4616fdf1ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6dc4b45f-fb0a-5a91-a655-10cf8d047d8b" :question/problem "![Directed segments: C_1: B to A; C_2: C to B; C_3: A to C](images/35/35be973517dc028556a314ea1ca3a1cb9a461cc2c06c17d30b4a9697bef160e0.png)\n\nThe arrows show the orientations of the segments. The same continuous vector field $\\mathbf F$ is used throughout. The closed path $C$ follows $A\\to B\\to C\\to A$ **counterclockwise**. Which expression equals the following line integral?\n\n$$\n\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "Trace the requested traversal. $C_1$ is reversed. $C_2$ is reversed. $C_3$ is reversed. Reversal negates a vector line integral, and additivity gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=\\int_{-C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{-C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{-C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\\\&=-\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708650 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e286dd1-b28e-57d9-bc32-d2e165f66fb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708645} {:answer/id #uuid "6218468d-a4d4-57b7-bc23-53433f8f0929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r