} {:answer/id #uuid "8ce4874e-a4a0-5a6c-aee4-96ab86686b4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708652} {:answer/id #uuid "9720bf96-36e2-5edf-a795-5e4106f6983a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708656} {:answer/id #uuid "ace3460d-becf-50e2-a09d-cc0a23b0d4db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708659}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708659} :answer-field/id #uuid "9553fcea-2d25-579c-a75a-09e5c2449639" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708655}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d52fd287-22e0-523f-8b51-691f9c4aa38e" :question/problem "![Directed segments: C_1: A to B; C_2: B to C; C_3: A to C](images/9d/9dd3f252121ae1d8b2c4df4a0297a243b57ea0b8fc891c915f75ce23f9af8801.png)\n\nThe arrows show the orientations of the segments. The same continuous vector field $\\mathbf F$ is used throughout. The closed path $C$ follows $A\\to C\\to B\\to A$ **clockwise**. Which expression equals the following line integral?\n\n$$\n\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "Trace the requested traversal. $C_1$ is reversed. $C_2$ is reversed. $C_3$ is followed. Reversal negates a vector line integral, and additivity gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=\\int_{-C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{-C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\\\&=-\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708672 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea8ab648-438d-5053-947d-ce148b59dbca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708682}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708682} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2382977-e3a8-5771-acba-77b2005a7d2b" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "08be80cc-abd6-5508-9c37-969a45df801b" :question/problem "![Directed segments: C_1: D to C; C_2: B to C; C_3: D to A; C_4: B to A; C_5: A to C](images/54/5480c83b384f2abd235cdb9b380bd5a75f15a0de271692c288b5c93b340231da.png)\n\nThe arrows show the orientations of the segments. The same continuous vector field $\\mathbf F$ is used throughout. Let $L_1$ follow $A\\to B\\to C\\to A$ and $L_2$ follow $A\\to D\\to C\\to A$. You are given\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{L_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=5\\\\\\int_{L_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe closed path $C$ follows $A\\to B\\to C\\to D\\to A$ **counterclockwise**. This path is the **outer boundary**. Evaluate its line integral.\n\n$\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=$ {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Write $I_j=\\int_{C_j}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$ for each segment in its arrow direction. Trace both named loops in their given directions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{L_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=I_2-I_4-I_5\\\\\\int_{L_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=I_1-I_3-I_5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe requested outer traversal has signed sum\n\n$$\n\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=-I_1+I_2+I_3-I_4\n$$\n\nChoose the loop orientations so that their shared diagonal cancels and the outer segments have those signs:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=(I_2-I_4-I_5)-(I_1-I_3-I_5)\\\\&=\\int_{L_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{L_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\\\&=(5)-(-3)\\\\&=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis uses orientation reversal and additivity; a closed path alone does not imply a zero integral."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708674 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c922ea2-00e4-5057-b4de-454c3819ee06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708676}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708676} :answer-field/id #uuid "4931e0a7-11e1-5cd0-9e59-9697a1710eb9" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708673}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5cd2aa58-4ecd-5f0c-84cf-56cd93d9cf08" :question/problem "![Directed segments: C_1: D to A; C_2: A to B; C_3: B to C; C_4: D to C; C_5: C to A](images/a1/a14ec792c3924723ca962f3921cd836bc3ddf012f4485bb447da2ca8cae10f15.png)\n\nThe arrows show the orientations of the segments. The same continuous vector field $\\mathbf F$ is used throughout. Let $L_1$ follow $A\\to B\\to C\\to A$ and $L_2$ follow $A\\to C\\to D\\to A$. You are given\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{L_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=-3\\\\\\int_{L_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe closed path $C$ follows $A\\to D\\to C\\to B\\to A$ **clockwise**. This path is the **outer boundary**. Evaluate its line integral.\n\n$\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=$ {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Write $I_j=\\int_{C_j}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$ for each segment in its arrow direction. Trace both named loops in their given directions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{L_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=I_2+I_3+I_5\\\\\\int_{L_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=I_1-I_4-I_5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe requested outer traversal has signed sum\n\n$$\n\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=-I_1-I_2-I_3+I_4\n$$\n\nChoose the loop orientations so that their shared diagonal cancels and the outer segments have those signs:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=-(I_2+I_3+I_5)-(I_1-I_4-I_5)\\\\&=-\\int_{L_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r-\\int_{L_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\\\&=-(-3)-(-2)\\\\&=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis uses orientation reversal and additivity; a closed path alone does not imply a zero integral."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708679 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e021d1f-f8e6-5d24-b41e-b67094c5ade9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708675}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708675} :answer-field/id #uuid "9729442b-4fd6-5e7c-91be-7e37f2f65ef2" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708678}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9e94c35d-a1a2-57d6-881a-a62fa9a3dcaf" :question/problem "![Directed segments: C_1: A to B; C_2: A to D; C_3: C to D; C_4: B to C; C_5: A to C](images/f3/f336318d756a33f21dba0dba2bd52aaff23d8b266cec2c4f031bf7ef695dd080.png)\n\nThe arrows show the orientations of the segments. The same continuous vector field $\\mathbf F$ is used throughout. Let $L_1$ follow $A\\to C\\to B\\to A$ and $L_2$ follow $A\\to C\\to D\\to A$. You are given\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{L_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=4\\\\\\int_{L_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe closed path $C$ follows $A\\to B\\to C\\to D\\to A$ **counterclockwise**. This path is the **outer boundary**. Evaluate its line integral.\n\n$\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=$ {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Write $I_j=\\int_{C_j}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$ for each segment in its arrow direction. Trace both named loops in their given directions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{L_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=-I_1-I_4+I_5\\\\\\int_{L_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=-I_2+I_3+I_5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe requested outer traversal has signed sum\n\n$$\n\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=I_1-I_2+I_3+I_4\n$$\n\nChoose the loop orientations so that their shared diagonal cancels and the outer segments have those signs:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=-(-I_1-I_4+I_5)+(-I_2+I_3+I_5)\\\\&=-\\int_{L_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{L_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\\\&=-(4)+(0)\\\\&=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis uses orientation reversal and additivity; a closed path alone does not imply a zero integral."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708680 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c668ff13-dd3d-5654-ad18-6b8d1313aa9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708681}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708681} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a66b3c9-33f5-515c-95c0-3306577825c7" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708677}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a84e093f-4b4e-5bab-8c34-191952b0d2ad" :question/problem "![Directed segments: C_1: C to B; C_2: D to A; C_3: C to D; C_4: C to A; C_5: B to A](images/ca/ca44141368bac2cbba7ced4f762c7502e41fa94dff30ce4eebf4876603feb33e.png)\n\nThe arrows show the orientations of the segments. The same continuous vector field $\\mathbf F$ is used throughout. Let $L_1$ follow $A\\to B\\to C\\to A$ and $L_2$ follow $A\\to C\\to D\\to A$. You are given\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{L_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=-1\\\\\\int_{L_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe closed path $C$ follows $A\\to B\\to C\\to D\\to A$ **counterclockwise**. This path is the **outer boundary**. Evaluate its line integral.\n\n$\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=$ {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Write $I_j=\\int_{C_j}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$ for each segment in its arrow direction. Trace both named loops in their given directions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{L_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=-I_1+I_4-I_5\\\\\\int_{L_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=I_2+I_3-I_4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe requested outer traversal has signed sum\n\n$$\n\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=-I_1+I_2+I_3-I_5\n$$\n\nChoose the loop orientations so that their shared diagonal cancels and the outer segments have those signs:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=(-I_1+I_4-I_5)+(I_2+I_3-I_4)\\\\&=\\int_{L_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r+\\int_{L_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r\\\\&=(-1)+(-3)\\\\&=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis uses orientation reversal and additivity; a closed path alone does not imply a zero integral."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708684 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e22fdcf0-3326-5f51-9e5a-7755effe39c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708691}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708691} :answer-field/id #uuid "c774a1d3-ee7b-5a6e-bb09-ef5cfb4e1b95" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1a05c95a-d7a3-5b6c-b26a-da0339527a48" :question/problem "![Directed segments: C_1: A to B; C_2: C to B; C_3: A to C](images/aa/aa0c4824cd83fc9db89a280bc804427adabf51610a1d62b39d1a7292ac16bb2e.png)\n\nThe arrows show the orientations of the segments. The same continuous vector field $\\mathbf F$ is used throughout. The closed path $C$ follows $A\\to B\\to C\\to A$ **counterclockwise**. You are given\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=6\\\\\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=6\\\\\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the integral along $C_3$ in the direction of its arrows.\n\n$\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=$ {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Write $I_j=\\int_{C_j}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$ for each segment in its arrow direction. Compare each arrow with the requested traversal. Reversed segments contribute negative integrals. By additivity,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=I_1-I_2-I_3\\\\6&=(6)-(2)-I_3\\\\6&=-I_3+4\\\\-I_3&=2\\\\I_3&=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final value is in the requested arrow direction."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708685 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7cd76ba-2e0f-5043-b102-12a16784aec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708690}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186708690} :answer-field/id #uuid "779fd801-1003-5cb5-9a70-9bbd45f8a99b" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186708687}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5ed01d7f-8d1b-5a5a-81f9-7cf612e1e099" :question/problem "![Directed segments: C_1: A to B; C_2: B to C; C_3: C to A](images/38/38a4b8304ca0a8122168f6e01824a13e899daaeb9b1b71e5f0320323d5ee78c1.png)\n\nThe arrows show the orientations of the segments. The same continuous vector field $\\mathbf F$ is used throughout. The closed path $C$ follows $A\\to B\\to C\\to A$ **counterclockwise**. You are given\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=0\\\\\\int_{C_1}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=0\\\\\\int_{C_3}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the integral along $C_2$ in the direction of its arrows.\n\n$\\int_{C_2}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r=$ {{answer}}" :question/worked-solution "Write $I_j=\\int_{C_j}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r$ for each segment in its arrow direction. Compare each arrow with the requested traversal. Reversed segments contribute negative integrals. By additivity,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{C}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathrm d\\mathbf r&=I_1+I_2+I_3\\\\0&=(0)+I_2+(-3)\\\\0&=I_2-3\\\\I_2&=3\\\\I_2&=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final value is in the requested arrow direction."}]}
